{#- The one clickable surface for anything that is not running text: a
    labelled action, a bare icon, a directional link. Two macros, one for
    each element a button can honestly be — an <a> that goes somewhere, or a
    <button> that does something here — so nothing has to decide by hand
    whether typing "btn" on a class list is enough to make something a
    button; this is the only place that decides it.

    Content is supplied by the caller through {% call %} rather than a
    label parameter, since a button's inside ranges from a single span to
    the two-line block adjacent navigation needs — only the outer element
    and its modifiers are standardised, not what a reader sees inside it. -#}

{% macro link(href, extra="", download=false, rel="", data="", ariaLabel="") %}
<a class="btn{% if extra %} {{ extra }}{% endif %}" href="{{ href }}"{% if download %} download{% endif %}{% if rel %} rel="{{ rel }}"{% endif %}{% if data %} {{ data }}{% endif %}{% if ariaLabel %} aria-label="{{ ariaLabel }}"{% endif %}>{{ caller() }}</a>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro action(extra="", data="", ariaLabel="") %}
<button type="button" class="btn{% if extra %} {{ extra }}{% endif %}"{% if data %} {{ data }}{% endif %}{% if ariaLabel %} aria-label="{{ ariaLabel }}"{% endif %}>{{ caller() }}</button>
{% endmacro %}
